    "content": "President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud has signed the ratification of the African Continental Free Trade Area (AfCFTA) agreement, formally completing Somalia's accession to the continental trade bloc. The signature followed parliamentary approval of the agreement. Somalia will now submit the official ratification documents to the African Union Commission, finalizing its membership.\n\nThe AfCFTA aims to create a single continental market for goods and services, eliminate tariffs on 90% of products, and reduce non-tariff barriers. Somalia's entry into the agreement is expected to benefit the country's traders, investors, manufacturers, cooperatives, and exporters by providing access to a market of over 1.3 billion people with a combined GDP of $3.4 trillion.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development signals enhanced opportunities for investment and trade linkages between Somalia and other African nations. Somali-owned businesses abroad may find new channels for sourcing goods and expanding operations within the continent, potentially reducing reliance on traditional trading partners.\n\nThe ratification is a key step in Somalia's economic integration with the region, following years of preparation and negotiations. The government has emphasized that the agreement will help diversify the economy, increase exports, and attract foreign direct investment.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/07/30/soomaaliya-oo-si-rasmi-ah-ugu-biirtay-heshiiska-ganacsiga-xorta-ah-ee-afrika-afcfta/",
